.²1 <ab>N.</ab> of a medicinal plant, Sidonia Cordifolia and Rhombifolia (<lang>Mar.</lang> <ns>{#cikaRA, cikaRI#}</ns>)
.²2 <ab>N.</ab> of a powerful charm or lore taught by Viśvāmitra to Rāma:-- {#gfhARa#}
 {#dve ime vidye balAmatibalAM taTA . na te Sramo jarA''vAByAM BavitA nANgavEkftam#}
 {#.. na ca suptaM pramattaM vA Darzayizyanti nErftAH . na ca te sadfSo rAma#}
 {#vIryeRAnyo Bavizyati .. sadevanaranAgezu lokezviha pumAMstrizu . na sOBAgye#}
 {#na dAkziRye na budDiSrutipOruze .. nottare pratipattavye tvattulyo vA#}
 {#Bavizyati . etadvidyAdvayaM prApya yaSaScAvyayamApsyasi .. balAmatibalAM#}
 {#cEva jYAnavijYAnamAtarO . kzutpipAse ca te rAma nAtyarTaM pIqayizyataH#}
 {#.. jayaSca durgakAntArapradeSezvawavIzu ca . sAratAM trizu lokezu gamizyasi#}
 {#ca rAGava .. pitAmahasute hyete vidye cAyurbalAvahe .#} <ls>Rām. 1. 22</ls>.
 See {#tO balAtibalayoH praBAvato#} <ls>R. 11. 9</ls> also.
.²3 <ab>N.</ab> of one of Dakṣaʼs daughters.
